<!-- SERVICE DEPTH -->
<section class="cx-problem cx-section" id="service-depth">
  <div class="cx-container">
    <div class="r">
      <div class="cx-eyebrow">What Each Service Actually Covers</div>
      <h2 class="cx-h2">Specifics matter.<br>Here is what is included.</h2>
      <p class="cx-sub" style="max-width:600px">Other contractors list service names. We list what we actually do — because the difference between a good project and a frustrating one lives in the details.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cx-problem-grid stagger">
      <div class="cx-problem-card r">
        <h3>Demolition</h3>
        <p>Full strip-outs, selective demo, hoarding installation, debris removal, bin management, rough cleaning, structural condition reporting, coordination with building management. We leave the space ready for the next trade — not just empty.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cx-problem-card r">
        <h3>Steel Framing</h3>
        <p>Light gauge steel partition framing, door openings, backing at specified heights, header installation, blocking for wall-mounted items, coordination with MEP rough-in. Our framing crew is in-house — not a sub who shows up two days late.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cx-problem-card r">
        <h3>Drywall &amp; Ceilings</h3>
        <p>Hang, tape, and multi-coat finish. Level 4 finish as standard on commercial applications. T-bar ceiling grids, bulkheads, soffits, acoustic tile, specialty ceilings. We do not leave taping for the painter to sand down.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cx-problem-card r">
        <h3>Finishing</h3>
        <p>Primer, paint (2-coat minimum), accent walls, trim installation, base and door casing, LVP and carpet flooring, tile, epoxy floors for industrial applications. Finish schedule managed against the approved specifications.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cx-problem-card r">
        <h3>Millwork &amp; Installation</h3>
        <p>Custom reception desks, office built-ins, break room cabinetry, credenzas, shelving, feature walls, signage substrates. Shop fabricated to spec, delivered on the date calculated at project start — not whenever the shop gets around to it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cx-problem-card r">
        <h3>Trade Coordination</h3>
        <p>Full MEP sequencing, sub scheduling and re-scheduling, daily site management, permit management, inspection coordination, conflict resolution, progress reporting. The work does not fall through the cracks because one person owns the whole picture.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

